WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.410
IRON MAIDEN is the only rock band with its
own private jet.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.880
And who do you think is the pilot?

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:17.510
Yes, nobody else but their lead singer, Bruce Dickinson.

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:20.480
And oh do few people deserve more admiration than Mr. Dickinson.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.310
If it wasn’t enough to be one of the most
successful heavy metal singers in history,

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.310
he’s also an

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:30.460
experienced commercial pilot, a radio host,
a writer, an entrepreneur AND the CEO of one

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:31.460
the most

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:32.610
innovative aviation companies.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:33.980
And now you might wonder…

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.870
Why are we talking about Bruce Dickinson on
VisualPolitik?

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:41.180
What does Iron Maiden have to do with politics?

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:42.640
Well…

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:49.050
IRON MAIDEN Singer BRUCE DICKINSON's CARDIFF
AVIATION Signs On To Manage National Carrier

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:50.050
For Djibouti

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:53.820
Cardiff Aviation is a company that provides
maintenance to airline companies.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.390
We could say that Iron Maiden has landed in
Djibouti but, in this case, they didn’t

00:00:58.390 --> 00:00:59.610
come to perform.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:04.329
They came to sell airplanes, train the pilots
and design a system so that Djibouti can have

00:01:04.329 --> 00:01:05.329
its own

00:01:05.329 --> 00:01:06.329
airlines.

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:10.220
But wait a minute because this is the really
important thing!

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:13.540
You might think the airlines of a country
like Djibouti aren’t a big deal, right?

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.130
We’re talking about a poor country, located
in the Horn of Africa, with a population of

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.130
less than a

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.219
million inhabitants.

00:01:20.219 --> 00:01:29.079
However… what if I told you that Djibouti
has a big chance of becoming the new DUBAI?

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:33.889
What if Bruce Dickinson is one of the first
visionaries to decide to invest in this country?

00:01:33.889 --> 00:01:35.900
Think about it while you look at this map.

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:37.130
Here it is.

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:38.130
DJIBOUTI.

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.770
This here is the SUEZ CANAL and this is the
RED SEA.

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:45.320
Any oil tanker who wants to go from ABU DHABI
to Europe must go through here.

00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.759
All of those Chinese mobile phones sold in
the UK travel through this area.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:54.569
1 out of 10 ships that sail the planet are
passing in front of the Djiboutian costs.

00:01:54.569 --> 00:01:56.960
But make no mistake, this is not a quiet region.

00:01:56.960 --> 00:01:58.529
In fact, the opposite is true.

00:01:58.529 --> 00:02:00.210
Have you ever heard of the Somali pirates?

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:01.929
Well, this is Somalia.

00:02:01.929 --> 00:02:05.549
And this country, Eritrea, isn’t a chill
place either.

00:02:05.549 --> 00:02:09.380
And this other place you see on the map…
this is called Yemen as is in the-middle-of-a-civil-war

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:10.380
Yemen.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:16.140
So as it turns out, Djibouti is the only peaceful
country in the whole region!!!

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:20.950
But hold on a minute because there’s still
more!!!

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:24.950
If you’ve been following VisualPolitik for
a long time, you should already know that

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.030
Ethiopia is one of

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:28.820
the fastest growing countries on the planet.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:31.020
They are becoming a textile superpower.

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.530
And they have more than 90 million inhabitants.

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:35.530
And guess what!

00:02:35.530 --> 00:02:37.400
Ethiopia has no coast!

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:42.280
This means, whenever they want to sell their
textiles, they have to do so through the Djibouti

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:43.280
port.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.470
And yes, I know what you’re thinking now.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:51.470
Are we really talking about a new Singapore
or Dubai or is there something missing here?

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:55.870
Should we be like Bruce Dickinson and start investing in Djibouti?

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:01.380
Today we are going to answer those questions but before we do, let’s take a look back

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:04.980
at history.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:08.640
LOCATION, LOCATION, LOCATION!

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:12.540
After everything I said about Djibouti, many
of you might be thinking how it’s possible

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.540
that we haven’t

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:15.100
heard of this country before, right?

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:21.720
The answer lies in their history, which is
no different from their neighbours.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:28.300
In the year 1977, after a peaceful referendum,
Djibouti became the latest country to gain

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.300
independence

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:30.950
from their French colonizers.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:37.040
And just as it happened in similar cases,
Djibouti became a one party dictatorship.

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:45.940
Until the 90s, Mr. HASSAN GOULED APTIDON and the other members of his tribe controlled

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.050
the fate of this

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:48.050
country.

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:53.390
Torturing members of the opposition became
a common practice and the ruling party got

00:03:53.390 --> 00:03:54.390
rich off of the

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:55.390
port’s profits.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:04:01.240
Back then, you could say Djibouti was a textbook
example of a GATE-KEEPER STATE.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:06.440
You see, in such poor countries, the whole
economy is dependent on just one thing.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:09.730
In the case of Equatorial Guinea, for instance,
that thing is oil.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:16.169
In the case of Djibouti, it’s the port.

00:04:16.169 --> 00:04:20.561
Since the dictators have no money to pay a
big army to control the whole country, they

00:04:20.561 --> 00:04:21.940
must focus all

00:04:21.940 --> 00:04:25.430
their oppressive powers in the areas where
the money is.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:30.630
So Djibouti’s port was completely secured
while the rest of the country was in total

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:31.879
chaos, with murders

00:04:31.879 --> 00:04:37.319
on the streets, rape and all kinds of other
crimes.

00:04:37.319 --> 00:04:43.860
As you can imagine, this is not the ideal
situation to create companies or attract foreign

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:44.860
investment.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:48.520
Now add in the fact that, in the 90s, a civil
war started between the Government and the

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.520
opposition

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.520
parties and tribes.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:59.370
AND 
this is where the first difference between

00:04:59.370 --> 00:05:03.139
Djibouti and the rest of their neighbours
comes in.

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:07.150
The way the government solved their problem
was surprising to everyone.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:11.479
Basically, after years of bloody fighting
and thousands of killings on both sides of

00:05:11.479 --> 00:05:12.710
the battle, Mr. APTIDON

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:17.419
went to the other party, the so-called,
“Front for the Restoration of Unity and

00:05:17.419 --> 00:05:19.090
Democracy”, and

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:21.409
told them ‘Hey fellas!

00:05:21.409 --> 00:05:23.449
Get a grip, there’s money for everyone here!

00:05:23.449 --> 00:05:25.199
Why don’t we share it so we can stop

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:26.570
fighting each other!?’

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:31.889
And this is how Djibouti got its first Unity
Government: A government that combined most

00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:33.039
of the local

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:34.650
political parties.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:40.779
Of course, there’s still political opposition
in Djibouti.

00:05:40.779 --> 00:05:45.720
But they can hardly make campaigns and anytime
there are presidential elections, they’re

00:05:45.720 --> 00:05:46.720
boycotted.

00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:51.249
This explains why APTIDON and, later on, his
nephew, OMAR GUELLEH, win the elections with

00:05:51.249 --> 00:05:52.249
outcomes close

00:05:52.249 --> 00:05:54.580
to 100% of the vote.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.550
Yes, very democratic, right?

00:05:57.550 --> 00:05:59.720
But this is just the beginning!

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:04.800
Despite the internal fights, by the year 2001,
Djibouti was still a very corrupt country

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:06.009
with a very weak

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:07.710
position.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:12.099
Think about it… we are talking about a very
small country, with less than 1 million inhabitants,

00:06:12.099 --> 00:06:13.099
placed

00:06:13.099 --> 00:06:16.219
in the middle of one of the most violent regions
on the planet.

00:06:16.219 --> 00:06:23.199
Next to them there’s SOMALIA, which is,
virtually, an anarchy where different tribes

00:06:23.199 --> 00:06:24.199
are constantly at

00:06:24.199 --> 00:06:25.870
each other’s throats.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:30.800
On the other side, we have ERITREA, a dictatorship
that makes North Korea look like Sweden.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:35.910
And in the South there’s Ethiopia, the biggest
regional power and one who, at any moment,

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:36.910
would be happy

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:38.999
to invade Djibouti so they can have the coast
line.

00:06:38.999 --> 00:06:43.680
So, in summary, they were far from being in
a quiet situation.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.719
But then, when everything seemed to be

00:06:45.719 --> 00:06:50.930
against them, history decided to give Djiboutians
a break.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:57.610
“Our enemy is a radical network of terrorists
and everyone who supports them”

00:06:57.610 --> 00:07:04.369
All of a sudden, America, with George W Bush
as their president, declared war on terrorismo.

00:07:04.369 --> 00:07:08.990
This meant sending troops to all the areas
with Al Qaeda cells.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:12.189
Which includes, of course, the Horn of Africa.

00:07:12.189 --> 00:07:15.740
And is there any better place for building
military bases than Djibouti?

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:20.809
It has a peerless location and a government
that, corrupted as it is, congratulates itself

00:07:20.809 --> 00:07:21.809
for being

00:07:21.809 --> 00:07:24.259
stable and having no ties with terrorist groups.

00:07:24.259 --> 00:07:30.369
Do you remember when I told you that the Red
Sea is extremely dangerous for merchant ships?

00:07:30.369 --> 00:07:33.779
From the CAMP LEMMONIER base, American troops
can chase those Somali pirates.

00:07:33.779 --> 00:07:36.139
And not only the Americans!

00:07:36.139 --> 00:07:39.589
In just 10 years, the list of countries who
have installed military bases in Djibouti

00:07:39.589 --> 00:07:45.430
is never-ending.

00:07:45.430 --> 00:07:48.729
We can find French, Italian and Spanish troops
there.

00:07:48.729 --> 00:07:52.770
The only place where Japan has a military
base abroad is Djibouti.

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:58.270
And, as you can imagine, with so many world
powers having a military presence here…

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:00.889
China should come

00:08:00.889 --> 00:08:03.110
into the picture too!

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.319
China opens first overseas base in Djibouti

00:08:05.319 --> 00:08:12.279
And, of course, in such a poor and small country,
having so many foreign armies is a great deal.

00:08:12.279 --> 00:08:16.619
Think about it, all those soldiers need to
eat somewhere, do their shopping and have

00:08:16.619 --> 00:08:17.619
some fun.

00:08:17.619 --> 00:08:20.759
This means lots of jobs and money for the
whole country.

00:08:20.759 --> 00:08:29.789
And on the top of it, this solves the biggest
problem Djibouti had for investment.

00:08:29.789 --> 00:08:34.020
With so many military bases in the country,
only a wacko would dare to invade them.

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:38.370
In fact, there are few places in Africa that
are safer than Djibouti nowadays.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:42.190
Add to this the perfect situation for international
trade routes and you can easily understand

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:43.190
why this

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:48.270
country has been growing at a 5% annual rate
since the day American troops put their boots

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:49.490
on the ground.

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:54.740
But as you might have guessed, not everything
is so wonderful here.

00:08:54.740 --> 00:08:59.160
Despite its recent growth, Djibouti still
has an unemployment rate higher than 50%.

00:08:59.160 --> 00:09:04.690
Yep, you heard that right, 1 out of 2 Djiboutians
has no stable job.

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:08.310
In other words, these airlines that Bruce
Dickinson helped create are just sending soldiers

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.310
and people

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:13.390
from NGOs that travel to places like Somalia
or Ethiopia.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:20.190
But wait a minute because the times are changing
in Djibouti!

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.950
A MAN AND HIS VISION

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:27.350
Remember this name, ILYAS MOUSSA DAWALEH.

00:09:27.350 --> 00:09:30.310
Do you think he’s their new President?

00:09:30.310 --> 00:09:31.310
Oh!

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.310
No!

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.310
No way!

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:36.240
Djibouti has kept the same President for the
past 20 years.

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.820
This man is the Minister of Economy and Finance.

00:09:39.820 --> 00:09:44.690
But, in this case, the finance minister is
even more famous than the president.

00:09:44.690 --> 00:09:48.450
We needed to plan over a longer period.

00:09:48.450 --> 00:09:51.100
We accept that we will probably not be able
to achieve all our

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:56.790
objectives during the current administration,
but Vision 2035 clearly sets out the aspirations

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:57.790
of the

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:00.410
President and his government
--ILYAS MOUSSA DAWALEH.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:05.150
If you’ve been following VisualPolitik for
a long time, this Vision 2035 thing will remind

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.150
you of

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:07.150
something…

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:09.590
Do you remember this video where I told you
about Rwanda’s road out of poverty?

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:14.640
Yes, this Vision 2035 is a carbon copy of
Rwanda’s plan in many aspects.

00:10:14.640 --> 00:10:18.550
The Djiboutian government wants their ports
to have state of the art technology just like

00:10:18.550 --> 00:10:19.550
those of

00:10:19.550 --> 00:10:22.210
Singapore and Dubai but, for this, they need
money.

00:10:22.210 --> 00:10:23.680
But not only that!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:30.050
Dawaleh knows that, in order to make the economy
work, you need to diversity it.

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:37.230
If a country only relies on one industry,
a single small crisis could easily be its

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.230
downfall.

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:42.450
Then again, if you wanna diversify your economy,
you still need money and a business friendly

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.450
environment.

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:48.180
And… corruption and lack of rule of law
are seldom friends of businesses and foreign

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.180
investment.

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:51.840
And in these areas, Djibouti has a gold medal.

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.870
For example, despite the port being the main
economic driver in this country, nobody can

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:56.870
see the

00:10:56.870 --> 00:10:57.870
accounting books.

00:10:57.870 --> 00:11:03.560
This means many Government officials are getting
rich without anyone knowing.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:09.170
If this wasn’t enough, part of the local
legislation is based on SHARIA LAW.

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:14.531
And nobody can even protest this because Djibouti
is among the 10 countries with the least freedom

00:11:14.531 --> 00:11:15.531
of

00:11:15.531 --> 00:11:16.531
speech in the entire world.

00:11:16.531 --> 00:11:22.370
Just in 2016, the Government sent 3 BBC journalists
to jail because they wanted to talk about

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:23.370
the

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:24.370
electoral fraud.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:26.660
As you can imagine, this is hurting this country’s
opportunities.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:31.190
And what’s worse… it is almost impossible
to change the system!

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:35.630
At the end of the day, the ruling class is
already making enough money from the port

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:36.630
and the rent they

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:40.440
get from all of those foreign armies.

00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:46.390
And they have enough security to not be scared
of a popular uprising.

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:49.570
In other words, if MOUSSA DAWALEH, the Djiboutian
finance minister, wanted to change the political

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:54.700
system, and, as he says on his Vision 2035
paper, ‘improve the governance of the country’

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:55.700
he has an

00:11:55.700 --> 00:11:57.110
impossible job… right?

00:11:57.110 --> 00:12:02.220
Well, my dear viewers, sometimes, miracles
happen.

00:12:02.220 --> 00:12:06.960
Djibouti breaks ground on massive Chinese-backed
free trade zone

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:11.510
In other words: if you can’t change the
whole political system in the entire country,

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:12.510
just change it in a

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:13.540
little part of it.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:17.790
In this special economic zone, everyone can
buy property and build without having to wait

00:12:17.790 --> 00:12:18.790
months and

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:20.040
months to get Government permission.

00:12:20.040 --> 00:12:24.880
This makes it harder for government officials
who want to get bribes.

00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:28.340
On the other hand, all the regulations will
follow Chinese law.

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:33.140
This is short of a little Shenzhen in the
middle of the country.

00:12:33.140 --> 00:12:40.390
The agreement calls for the zone to handle
$7 billion in trade within two years.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:41.390
Djibouti will create a

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:45.550
unified customs system with China, establish
a transit trade centre and set up a currency

00:12:45.550 --> 00:12:51.910
clearing system

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.040
So what can we expect now?

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:58.040
Well, the idea of making special economic
zones is nothing new.

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:59.800
And it’s been proven to work.

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:05.800
In fact, this is the system that let Dubai
become the big metropolis it is today.

00:13:05.800 --> 00:13:09.860
The idea is that, when you have a special
economic zone, both the citizens and the political

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:10.860
elite can

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:20.020
see firsthand what happens when you have transparent
laws and a good framework for companies.

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:24.490
If this experiment works, politicians will
be more willing to implement real changes

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:26.700
in Djibouti.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:31.560
In summary, we have an African country where
security is granted by foreign armies and

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:32.560
who is starting to

00:13:32.560 --> 00:13:34.160
apply serious reforms.

00:13:34.160 --> 00:13:39.000
A country with the perfect location and size
to become a financial and logistical centre

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.000
in one of the

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:41.380
busiest areas on the planet.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:46.720
It seems Mr. Dickinson found a virgin paradise
for investment, doesn’t it?

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:51.690
But hold on just a second because this does
not mean Djibouti is going to become a Freedom

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:52.690
and Human

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:53.930
Rights haven!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:58.240
At the end of the day, neither China nor Dubai
are such havens either.

00:13:58.240 --> 00:14:07.070
But this can be, at least, the beginning of
the end of poverty in the region.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:08.910
SO now the question is…

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.470
Do you think these positive predictions will
become true?

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:17.280
Is this a good time to invest in Djibouti
or will it all amount to nothing more than

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:18.370
hopeful predictions?

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.490
Please, leave your answer in the comment section
below.

